import Mathlib

/-!
# A note on cube-free problems

Source: https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.12318 (Yuchen Meng), abstract, Definitions 1.1 and 1.2,
Theorem 2.1 and Theorem 3.1 with the remark after its proof.
Credit: @ivillar

Abstract of the source: Eberhard and Pohoata conjectured that every $3$-cube-free subset of $[N]$
has size less than $2N/3+o(N)$. In this paper we show that if we replace $[N]$ with
$\mathbb{Z}_N$ the upper bound of $2N/3$ holds, and the bound is tight when $N$ is divisible by
$3$ since we have $A=\{a\in \mathbb{Z}_N : a\equiv 1,2 \pmod 3\}$.

Formalization notes:
* Definition 1.1 of the source: the projective $3$-cube generated by a multiset $\{x, y, z\}$ is
  the set of the sums over its nonempty subfamilies, $\{x, y, z, x+y, y+z, x+z, x+y+z\}$; the
  elements $x, y, z$ need not be distinct. Definition 1.2: $A$ is $3$-cube-free when it contains
  no projective $3$-cube.
* $\mathbb{Z}_N$ is `ZMod N` with `N` positive, and $|A| \le 2N/3$ is written `3 * A.card ≤ 2 * N`.
  As the source remarks after the proof of Theorem 3.1, the upper bound holds in every cyclic
  group, not only when $3 \mid N$; it is stated here for every positive `N`, as in the abstract.
* When $3 \mid N$ the residue of $a \in \mathbb{Z}_N$ modulo $3$ is well defined; it is read off
  the canonical representative `a.val`.
* `main` is the result that the abstract announces as proved (upper bound and tightness). The
  abstract also conjectures the analogous bound $(d-1)N/d$ for $d$-cube-free subsets of
  $\mathbb{Z}_N$ with $d \mid N$ (Conjecture 2 of the source); that conjecture is not asserted
  here.
-/

namespace OMA.S_arxiv_2311_12318

/-- The projective 3-cube generated by the multiset `{x, y, z}`. -/
def cube {N : ℕ} (x y z : ZMod N) : Set (ZMod N) :=
  {x, y, z, x + y, y + z, x + z, x + y + z}

/-- `A` is 3-cube-free: it contains no projective 3-cube. -/
def CubeFree {N : ℕ} (A : Set (ZMod N)) : Prop :=
  ∀ x y z : ZMod N, ¬ cube x y z ⊆ A

theorem main : ∀ (N : ℕ) [NeZero N],
    (∀ A : Finset (ZMod N), CubeFree (A : Set (ZMod N)) → 3 * A.card ≤ 2 * N) ∧
    (3 ∣ N → ∃ A : Finset (ZMod N),
      (∀ a : ZMod N, a ∈ A ↔ a.val % 3 = 1 ∨ a.val % 3 = 2) ∧
      CubeFree (A : Set (ZMod N)) ∧ 3 * A.card = 2 * N) := by
  sorry

end OMA.S_arxiv_2311_12318
